WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.260
Seeker: I'll bring out one of those. [glass clinking]

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:03.680
Delwath: Um,

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.520
Delwath: Delwath will just sort of stand a little bit back, like

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.920
Delwath: clearly a companion of Seeker, but not like-

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:13.900
Seeker: Mm-hmm

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:18.980
Delwath: ... not trying to present himself as a craftsman or part of the, like, um...

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:24.600
Delwath: But I'll try and cultivate a little bit of an air of, "When you're done, I have a question."

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.600
Seeker: So I'll, I'll put this object out on the table, and we'll get into queue to talk to her.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:28.180
DM: Well, there's like-

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:28.860
Seeker: She's-

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.860
DM: She's currently in the middle of... I mean, are you just gonna wait?

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:31.160
Seeker: Yeah.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.200
DM: What are you... Okay.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.400
Delwath: Well, I don't know. Yeah, I would just wait.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.020
Unknown: We'll, we'll, we'll sort of

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.260
Seeker: make ourselves known as we enter, but not interrupt.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:39.340
DM: Okay.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.960
DM: So you wait. She talks to this one person, and like, then she's in the way.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:46.480
DM: Um,

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.220
DM: talks to the next person and she's in the way.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:51.160
DM: Um,

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.420
DM: talks to the dwarf.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:58.340
DM: It's been like, I don't, I don't know, 45 minutes at this point.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:02.040
DM: Talks to the dwarf, like, she's in the way, and then kind of looks up,

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.040
DM: like, "Anyone else?"

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:09.920
Seeker: I stand, bringing myself to my full height, which is less, less than half of hers.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:10.860
DM: Yeah.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:12.740
Seeker: Um, and stride over,

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.580
Seeker: holding this glass and stone construction

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:22.680
Seeker: and a notebook in the other hand, and say, uh, "Greetings.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.080
Seeker: I come to you with curiosity."

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.580
DM: Don't recognize you.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:26.660
Seeker: I-

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:27.520
DM: You at the university?

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:31.880
Seeker: I, my name is Seeker, and I come with my friends from afar.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:32.960
DM: That's a pretentious name.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.040
Seeker: It is, in my view,

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:41.860
Seeker: the deepest type of humility because I come bearing questions.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:43.680
Delwath: It's not flattery.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:48.600
Seeker: Exactly. [laughs]

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.640
DM: Kind of, she cracks a slight smile at that.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:54.600
Seeker: Sometimes we find things.

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:56.300
Seeker: I am-

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.380
DM: So you're interested in learning?

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:02.980
Seeker: Always, but I am also a maker of things.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:06.220
Seeker: In some senses like you, though I do not work primarily in metals,

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.000
Seeker: as you can see.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:09.919
DM: She looks down.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.180
DM: She picks up like one of the...

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:16.060
DM: She like looks at one of the little glass constructions.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:19.000
DM: Not bad,

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.000
DM: but I'm not sure what I could teach you.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.740
Seeker: Thank you, and I think that there is much you could teach us.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.980
Seeker: My friends and I are especially interested in,

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:34.260
Seeker: uh, the energetic sources of fire,

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.820
Seeker: and especially things that volcanoes can do.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:40.260
DM: Why would I teach you that?

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:46.100
Seeker: Perhaps there is something that you could gain from us in exchange.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.760
DM: She looks down at your work.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:49.400
DM: Unlikely.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:51.240
Seeker: There's-

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:53.060
Delwath: [laughs]

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.860
Seeker: We have, and I look around at my friends, uh,

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.780
Seeker: collected a few other objects that might be of interest.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.020
Seeker: Are there things that you have

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:05.880
Seeker: a need for? Materials or-

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:06.240
DM: No

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:06.860
Seeker: ... uh, minerals,

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:08.560
Seeker: objects,

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:14.120
Seeker: perhaps even magical objects that might be hard to obtain?

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:16.720
Seeker: Any curiosities?

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:17.920
DM: Make a, make a persuasion check.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.980
Seeker: Seeker's not the most persuasive person.

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:23.620
Seeker: [die rolling]

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:24.540
Delwath: [laughs] 1.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:28.000
Unknown: We leave. [laughs] Oh, man.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:36.480
Seeker: See, that, that's a case where the, the situation and the die roll kind of harmonize a little bit.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:40.640
Seeker: [laughs]

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:43.000
DM: I think you're in the wrong place, dwarf friend.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:47.820
Seeker: Uh.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.540
DM: Bridgeward is where the market is.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:53.180
DM: I'm sure there is somebody who will buy your trinkets.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:03:58.240
Delwath: Um.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:01.820
DM: I deal in knowledge of metals, of which you seem to have little to offer.

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:02.600
Delwath: Hmm.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.560
Seeker: Oh, we never did sense ore at the cathedral.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:07.820
DM: Oh.

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:08.600
Seeker: That's okay.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:09.800
DM: Um, what were you looking to learn?

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:10.840
Seeker: So

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:18.740
Seeker: what it says is that you just find out what interesting stuff there is of a f- in a few types of, like, valuable-

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:19.000
DM: Right

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:24.520
Seeker: ... materials and uncut gems within 300 feet, and then I can pick one of those to investigate further if there's anything.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:25.060
DM: So

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:29.000
DM: yeah, I mean, then there, there...

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.400
DM: You wouldn't actually have sensed a lot of

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:35.480
DM: anything in the temple itself.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:36.620
DM: I mean, marble

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:40.920
DM: is nice, but it doesn't count as a...

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:42.900
DM: It's just stone, right?

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:43.360
Delwath: Mm-hmm.

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:50.760
DM: Um, and it wasn't... There's not like you sense some like, you know, secret diamond at the center of the temple or anything like that.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:56.680
DM: Um, and stuff in ch- like if it's blocked by wood or something, you can't sense it.

00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:02.260
DM: So if there's, you know, treasure in a chest or something, you wouldn't be able to tell, but.

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:08.440
Delwath: Um, when she says, "I seek, I deal in knowledge of metals," I'll like s- step forward a little bit.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:09.640
DM: Nice, nice.

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:10.540
Delwath: Um.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:12.560
Seeker: Yeah, t- jump in. [laughs]

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:12.740
Delwath: Uh, I'll-

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:14.240
Unknown: Person with proficiency in persuasion.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:16.880
Delwath: [laughs] I'll sort of, um,

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:18.240
Delwath: um,

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:21.000
Delwath: I'll sort of bow to her a little bit.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:21.580
Delwath: Um, and-

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:23.160
DM: Are you interested in being a student?

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:25.800
DM: You not quite look the type, although

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:29.220
DM: I deeply respect the craft of your people.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:30.040
Delwath: I

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:32.300
Delwath: humbly, uh,

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:36.400
Delwath: would never be qualified to work under you.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:37.700
Delwath: Your work is far too fine.

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:43.780
Delwath: I deal only in the ephemeral, foods and drinks and such-

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:44.800
