00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.700
Delwath: strange and unusual metals we have encountered on our travels.

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:03.400
Seeker: Oh, we have some adamantium still, or do we-

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:03.620
Delwath: Yeah

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:04.840
Seeker: ... no, you made it into armor?

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:12.620
Delwath: Yeah, I have an adamantine shield, and I have a strange piece of black metal that came from I don't know where that used to make my ado- armor shadow.

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:14.260
Seeker: Oh.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:15.040
DM: Oh, all right.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:16.340
Delwath: Extra dimensional metal. Sweet.

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:17.980
Seeker: You, you have weird mystery metal?

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:19.240
Delwath: I do have weird mystery metal.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:21.520
Seeker: Okay.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:22.320
Delwath: Possibly.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:27.560
Delwath: I'll take out the charred, uh, black metal.

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:28.240
Seeker: See, that's great.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:31.860
DM: She looks for a moment.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:38.820
Unknown: Like, she sort of reaches over as if like...

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:40.260
Delwath: I'll hand it to her.

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:43.880
DM: I've not seen this before.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.200
Unknown: Fascinating mysteries you present.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:49.320
DM: What was your name?

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:49.980
Delwath: Delwath.

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:50.600
DM: Delwath.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.840
Unknown: Interesting. Where did you come by this?

00:06:58.960 --> 00:06:59.340
Delwath: That is

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:02.660
Delwath: quite the s- I'll look around. Is there, like, still people listening?

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:05.620
DM: I mean, you're in the middle of a tavern.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:07.720
DM: Like, you know, if somebody was...

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:10.460
DM: There's not anybody super close.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:10.840
Delwath: Right

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:12.300
DM: ... but, like-

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:12.740
Delwath: Um

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:15.120
DM: ... it's not, the room is not empty.

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:15.820
Delwath: That is a

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:18.060
Delwath: long

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:25.580
Delwath: and somewhat private tale I would be welcome to tell you, but is there somewhere a little bit less, uh,

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:30.700
Delwath: open where I could share this tale with you?

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:33.380
Delwath: I'll also, I'll take out my ad- adamantine shield.

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:36.380
Delwath: We've also, I don't know if you've worked in this metal before.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:38.820
DM: Hmm.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:43.040
DM: Where did you come by this?

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:47.580
Delwath: A slightly less long and dark tale.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:48.380
Delwath: Uh,

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:51.680
Delwath: we found

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:53.940
Delwath: this in a

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:58.340
Delwath: fort, an old dwarven fort to the south of here.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:07:59.540
DM: Yeah.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:00.020
Delwath: Uh-

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:03.600
Wellby: Name it in its relation to the Stoneborn Village-

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:04.440
Delwath: Near-

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:04.540
DM: ... near there

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.020
Delwath: ... oh yeah, where did Dakrad come from?

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:07.020
Delwath: What was Dakrad's village?

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:08.600
DM: Uh, Kunda.

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:11.220
Delwath: Uh, just a little south of Kunda.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:14.120
DM: In a not such place.

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:16.520
Delwath: Uh, it is a village of your people in the

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:18.340
Delwath: mountains.

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:20.360
DM: Far away.

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:24.200
Delwath: Yes. But the, the dwarves mined it, I guess.

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:25.200
Delwath: I don't know its history.

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:27.040
Delwath: And a

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:33.520
Delwath: smith of some small talent was able to help me build it into a shield.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:37.040
Delwath: I no longer have use of such things as I've acquired a

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:40.860
Delwath: different shield more to my

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:42.700
Delwath: nature.

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:44.340
DM: She looks at the shield.

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:48.540
DM: The smith was at least a medium talent.

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:52.680
Delwath: If I ever see him again, I will pass along your compliments.

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:59.560
DM: [laughs] Um,

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:02.760
Unknown: m- uh, make a persuasion check.

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:13.080
Delwath: 24. [laughs]

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:13.320
DM: [laughs]

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:16.100
DM: I'll just, like, pat Seeker on the shoulder like, "It's okay,

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:18.360
Seeker: Seeker.

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:20.320
Delwath: We love you even if nobody else does."

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:21.400
Seeker: [laughs]

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:24.020
Delwath: Damn.

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:24.860
DM: Brutal.

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:25.920
DM: She

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:28.680
DM: waves over to, um,

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:33.220
DM: the barkeep and says something in Dwarven, which

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:39.500
DM: Seeker, you understand her really asking if his, um, if the back room is empty.

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:40.180
Delwath: Mm-hmm.

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:41.560
DM: And he's like, "Yeah,

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:45.280
DM: sure. You want some, you want some food, too?"

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:51.620
DM: She turns to you and she says, "Do not believe there are more

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.380
DM: interviews today.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:55.960
DM: Um,

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:02.740
DM: uh, the back room is available if you want to come with me."

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:03.440
Delwath: Of course.

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:08.080
DM: She motions for, um, the barkeep to bring some food and drinks as well.

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:11.240
Delwath: How many students do you have?

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:15.000
DM: Two right now.

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:19.580
DM: Hope to find a third, but there are so few worthy.

00:10:19.999 --> 00:10:24.700
Delwath: Hmm.

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:25.020
DM: Come.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:28.200
Delwath: So I'll, I'll,

00:10:30.140 --> 00:10:35.740
Delwath: I'll tell her the story of the, of the black metal, which if I remember correctly, I have no idea where it came from.

00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:37.200
Delwath: It just was in my armor when-

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:37.400
DM: Yeah

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:38.320
Delwath: ... yeah. So

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:43.680
Delwath: I'll basically tell her about, briefly about being on another plane for-

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:44.880
DM: She'd saw something

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:45.860
Delwath: ... quite a long time.

00:10:46.820 --> 00:10:56.940
Delwath: Um, and how when I awakened on Taelgar, this metal was embedded in my armor, and I don't know where it came from, but presumably that

00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:57.680
Delwath: other dimension.

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:02.700
DM: I mean, she spends 15 minutes just kind of looking at it.

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:08.460
DM: She takes out, like, a few little tools and, like, taps at it a little bit and, like, measures its hardness and things, and

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:12.760
DM: it's definitely extraplanar in origin.

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:17.480
Delwath: To insult it.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:20.740
DM: Um, I mean, she's like, you know,

00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:22.880
DM: a little

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:28.200
DM: reasonably, like, not super annoyed, but kind of like

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:37.680
DM: you can, you sort of get the sense, like, her desire to just go leave and not talk to people is more than her curiosity about-

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:37.920
Delwath: Yeah

00:11:39.100 --> 00:11:44.880
DM: ... these str- this, like, she's genuinely kind of amazed that there's a metal that she's never seen before.

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:46.400
Delwath: She cockle?

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:47.460
DM: No.

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:52.880
Delwath: [laughs] Is there anything we're trying to...

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:58.020
Delwath: No, anyway, I'm gonna, I'm gonna sort of, I'll tell her that we are,

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:02.220
Delwath: I'll tell her, you know, we don't wanna impose on her time.

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:07.600
Delwath: Obviously, she has more important things to do than talk to a motley collection of travelers.

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:11.550
Delwath: Um, but that we are- ...

00:12:11.590 --> 00:12:13.450
Delwath: heading to the Skaer Islands soon,

00:12:14.390 --> 00:12:14.770
Delwath: and

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:18.150
Delwath: I'll tell her I'd be welcome to leave these, um,

00:12:19.309 --> 00:12:22.130
Delwath: these, uh, metals with her for further study.

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:23.330
Delwath: Um,

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:28.270
Delwath: and if there's anything she can think of to, any uses she can think of,

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:32.770
Delwath: I would be glad to commission a work, uh, when we return.

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:34.210
Delwath: Um,

00:12:35.250 --> 00:12:36.750
Delwath: and then if there's any,

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:39.170
Delwath: uh, uh, if there's any

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:41.850
Delwath: advice she could give us,

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:44.870
Delwath: in particular, um-

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:47.970
Kenzo: About fire elements

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:50.030
Delwath: ... about, yeah, I'm just trying to think how to phrase it.

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:53.290
Delwath: Um, I'll sort of mention there's a, we have a hidden purpose.

