07:22:24.381 --> 07:22:26.901
DM: Oh, no- nothing moving around the caldera.

07:22:28.601 --> 07:22:31.541
Wellby: From the caldera, can I sneak to the edge and look down at the docks?

07:22:32.941 --> 07:22:34.261
DM: It's like a, it's like a mile.

07:22:34.261 --> 07:22:35.821
DM: It's like three-quarters a mile.

07:22:36.361 --> 07:22:39.021
DM: Like, it's a, it slopes down and it's a...

07:22:39.141 --> 07:22:39.221
Wellby: Hmm.

07:22:39.221 --> 07:22:40.721
Unknown: I mean, you can head in that direction.

07:22:42.041 --> 07:22:42.181
Wellby: Mm-hmm.

07:22:43.801 --> 07:22:49.201
Wellby: Yeah, I'll fly up high enough to look like a bird, seagull or something-ish.

07:22:49.621 --> 07:22:51.320
DM: Okay. Um, there is...

07:22:51.320 --> 07:22:53.301
DM: You do see, like, uh, some...

07:22:53.301 --> 07:22:57.401
DM: There's this longhouse there that's been burnt and the roof has collapsed.

07:22:57.401 --> 07:23:03.681
DM: And when you get, like, directly over it, like high enough that, um, it's not obvious, like, what you

07:23:04.841 --> 07:23:07.581
DM: are and look down, you can see that there's like some sort of

07:23:09.201 --> 07:23:12.841
DM: creatures kind of pawing around, like almost looking for bodies in there.

07:23:12.861 --> 07:23:15.361
DM: They're, like, not quite bipedal.

07:23:15.361 --> 07:23:21.301
DM: They're like, have huge mouths and they're like sort of digging in the dirt down there.

07:23:21.321 --> 07:23:21.441
Wellby: Hmm.

07:23:21.561 --> 07:23:23.241
DM: Some sort of undead-ish creature.

07:23:24.561 --> 07:23:28.061
Wellby: Something... Uh, is it possible to close the gates to the caldera?

07:23:28.781 --> 07:23:28.921
DM: Yeah.

07:23:29.521 --> 07:23:29.961
Wellby: I'll do that.

07:23:29.961 --> 07:23:30.701
Seeker: That's, that's a good idea.

07:23:32.001 --> 07:23:32.521
DM: Okay.

07:23:38.501 --> 07:23:40.661
Delwath: Um, should we, uh...

07:23:41.361 --> 07:23:43.781
Wellby: And then go through all the structures and just make sure it's all...

07:23:44.041 --> 07:23:44.081
Wellby: Yeah.

07:23:44.181 --> 07:23:45.621
DM: Like, I mean, if the caldera's at, like...

07:23:45.621 --> 07:23:47.021
DM: You should scout the whole...

07:23:47.021 --> 07:23:49.561
Delwath: If it's totally empty, I think we should just sleep here.

07:23:49.901 --> 07:23:50.361
Wellby: Yeah, I agree.

07:23:53.181 --> 07:23:55.021
Kenzo: Prepare ourself for the, uh, big battle.

07:23:56.341 --> 07:23:58.741
Delwath: Well, and we should probably go clear out the undead.

07:23:58.741 --> 07:24:00.361
Delwath: We should go see what's-

07:24:00.381 --> 07:24:00.941
Kenzo: Burn the bodies?

07:24:01.721 --> 07:24:04.081
Delwath: Like, well, I think we should, like...

07:24:04.081 --> 07:24:05.541
Delwath: I don't know. They might not be...

07:24:06.561 --> 07:24:10.861
Delwath: I mean, even the pirates could be, like, Waa-Skaer who fell into...

07:24:11.541 --> 07:24:13.621
Delwath: Right? I would, like, bury them.

07:24:14.701 --> 07:24:15.861
Delwath: Try and put them to rest.

07:24:17.041 --> 07:24:19.501
Wellby: I think burning the bodies would put them to rest.

07:24:20.281 --> 07:24:22.721
Delwath: Wellby's buried a mercenary a few times.

07:24:22.721 --> 07:24:25.101
Unknown: I think halflings, uh, don't bury.

07:24:25.621 --> 07:24:26.801
Delwath: Yeah, that probably makes sense.

07:24:27.801 --> 07:24:29.521
Delwath: It's like the memory carries them.

07:24:29.541 --> 07:24:29.741
Unknown: You don't-

07:24:29.841 --> 07:24:29.981
Wellby: Right

07:24:29.981 --> 07:24:30.781
Wellby: ... the body needs to be-

07:24:30.821 --> 07:24:33.541
Wellby: And that they're also, you know, because they're nomadic.

07:24:33.841 --> 07:24:35.621
Delwath: Right. There's like no... Yeah.

07:24:36.481 --> 07:24:37.601
Seeker: But also, like, uh-

07:24:39.931 --> 07:24:46.631
Kenzo: You know, we're about to put this fucking powerful scepter thing that, like, controls all kinds of other shit and-

07:24:46.671 --> 07:24:50.811
Wellby: I mean, w- we didn't get to this level by not burning the dead bodies of our enemies.

07:24:50.811 --> 07:24:51.151
Wellby: [laughs]

07:24:51.171 --> 07:24:53.071
Unknown: You're not wrong. You're not wrong.

07:24:53.131 --> 07:25:03.391
Kenzo: And also, it's like we put the scepter in at, in two days or 48 hours time for a day, and that unleashes

07:25:03.391 --> 07:25:07.531
Kenzo: some super powerful fucking ultra demon that we have to then have to fight.

07:25:08.131 --> 07:25:10.411
Unknown: Well, w- what if, though, and-

07:25:10.431 --> 07:25:10.571
Unknown: What if

07:25:10.571 --> 07:25:12.171
Unknown: ... and Wellby will say this. Well, what if

07:25:13.131 --> 07:25:14.991
Unknown: we're actually doing the demon a favor?

07:25:15.751 --> 07:25:21.131
Wellby: It's been trapped in this thing for thousands of years, forced to power it, and we're doing it a favor.

07:25:21.131 --> 07:25:25.991
Wellby: We're freeing it. We could offer to banish it back to its home dimension again.

07:25:25.991 --> 07:25:26.831
Wellby: That's true.

07:25:26.831 --> 07:25:28.091
Wellby: Give it a free trip home.

07:25:28.091 --> 07:25:29.391
Wellby: Like everybody wins.

07:25:29.631 --> 07:25:30.451
Delwath: I love that.

07:25:30.451 --> 07:25:31.751
Wellby: I think it's at least worth a shot.

07:25:31.751 --> 07:25:32.631
Kenzo: I love that.

07:25:32.631 --> 07:25:37.731
Delwath: And we can also magic circle, and it can't get out, and just stand far away

07:25:38.871 --> 07:25:39.931
Delwath: and then negotiate with it.

07:25:40.651 --> 07:25:43.731
Kenzo: I love that. I love that because having to do this shit again, that was-

07:25:43.731 --> 07:25:43.911
Unknown: [laughs]

07:25:43.911 --> 07:25:46.711
Kenzo: ... that was fucking crazy. That was, that was not fun.

07:25:46.711 --> 07:25:51.691
Kenzo: But whatever the hell is bound to that scepter is gonna be at least as powerful as the thing that we just killed.

07:25:51.731 --> 07:25:53.411
Delwath: But also conceptually,

07:25:55.131 --> 07:25:58.011
Delwath: if it's one thing and we're prepared for it to come out-

07:25:58.511 --> 07:25:58.831
Kenzo: Yeah

07:25:58.831 --> 07:26:02.231
Delwath: ... we know it's gonna come out, and we have a magic circle to trap it.

07:26:02.231 --> 07:26:03.811
Kenzo: And we control where it comes out.

07:26:03.811 --> 07:26:04.211
Delwath: Yeah.

07:26:04.211 --> 07:26:05.391
Wellby: We did well with the pirate guy.

07:26:06.571 --> 07:26:09.971
Delwath: And then, I mean, if nothing else, I could just cast Banish three times.

07:26:09.971 --> 07:26:13.411
Delwath: Actually, the magic circle lasts for four hours.

07:26:13.411 --> 07:26:15.551
Delwath: I cast Banish six times.

07:26:15.551 --> 07:26:17.951
Kenzo: So we put a magic circle around the scepter and then what?

07:26:17.971 --> 07:26:19.371
Delwath: I mean, it can still cast spells on us,

07:26:20.331 --> 07:26:24.031
Delwath: but we put a magic circle around the scepter that traps the demon.

07:26:24.031 --> 07:26:26.091
Delwath: We then basically offer to send it home.

07:26:26.651 --> 07:26:29.011
Kenzo: Well, but it's in the holy water too, which it probably doesn't like.

07:26:29.431 --> 07:26:29.871
Delwath: That's true.

07:26:30.351 --> 07:26:40.491
Wellby: Tim, do we get clarity about what the sequence is that does the demon come out when 24 hours in the holy water has elapsed or when we after that then smash the scepter, or do we know?

07:26:41.691 --> 07:26:41.911
Unknown: Um,

07:26:42.851 --> 07:26:43.211
Delwath: the,

07:26:46.411 --> 07:26:47.411
Delwath: the-

07:26:47.451 --> 07:26:48.071
Kenzo: The implication

07:26:48.071 --> 07:26:48.590
Wellby: ... the

07:26:49.631 --> 07:27:00.331
DM: holy, 24 hours in the holy water, um, loosens the connection, and if a demon is, or a devil is to emerge, it is when the scepter is actually destroyed.

07:27:00.331 --> 07:27:05.911
DM: But it, it's the 24 hours in the holy water, like, bakes it, so it can't protect the scepter anymore.

07:27:05.911 --> 07:27:09.031
Delwath: Wait, it, it, when it's actually destroyed, then it would emerge?

07:27:09.051 --> 07:27:10.271
Delwath: But we can destroy it in theory.

07:27:10.271 --> 07:27:11.691
Wellby: In the magic circle, yeah, yeah.

07:27:11.711 --> 07:27:13.891
Delwath: In theory, we can destroy it by hitting it with something heavy.

07:27:13.891 --> 07:27:15.331
Kenzo: Wait, wait, wait, wait.

07:27:15.331 --> 07:27:16.111
Seeker: But, but why would we not just-

07:27:16.131 --> 07:27:16.251
Wellby: The ladder can destroy it

07:27:16.251 --> 07:27:16.251
Unknown: ... drop it in the magic?

07:27:16.251 --> 07:27:16.251
Unknown: Wait.

07:27:16.251 --> 07:27:17.331
Wellby: The ladder can destroy it.

07:27:18.771 --> 07:27:19.991
Wellby: No, no. Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

07:27:19.991 --> 07:27:20.351
Seeker: That's an interesting thing.

07:27:20.351 --> 07:27:23.931
Kenzo: But why would we not at that point not just actually drop it into the fucking volcano?

07:27:23.971 --> 07:27:25.251
Delwath: Well, that's what I'm wondering, right?

07:27:25.251 --> 07:27:26.991
Delwath: That's not gonna be nice to a demon, right?

07:27:27.011 --> 07:27:27.471
Delwath: Like, the demon's-

07:27:27.491 --> 07:27:28.591
Wellby: Demons are immune to fire

07:27:28.591 --> 07:27:30.171
Kenzo: ... yeah. Uh, okay.

07:27:30.851 --> 07:27:32.131
Kenzo: Well, then that will not be useful.

07:27:32.891 --> 07:27:36.491
Kenzo: Where could we, where could we destroy it that would m- be maximally harmful to it?

07:27:38.291 --> 07:27:40.311
Unknown: I mean, holy water.

07:27:40.311 --> 07:27:41.011
Seeker: Like where we are?

07:27:41.151 --> 07:27:42.811
Delwath: Where we are, like literally right here.

07:27:42.811 --> 07:27:44.751
Unknown: Yeah. So we destroy the scepter inside-

07:27:44.791 --> 07:27:46.651
Wellby: Wait, wait, wait. If we... It can't get out of a magic circle?

07:27:46.851 --> 07:27:47.171
Delwath: Yeah.

07:27:47.231 --> 07:27:50.611
Wellby: Can you cast a magic circle while the scepter is in the pool of holy water?

07:27:50.651 --> 07:27:50.751
Unknown: Yes.

07:27:50.751 --> 07:27:51.191
Wellby: Yeah.

07:27:51.191 --> 07:27:52.991
Wellby: So it's stuck in the pool of holy water?

07:27:53.031 --> 07:27:53.111
Unknown: Yes.

07:27:53.111 --> 07:27:53.391
Kenzo: Yeah.

07:27:53.411 --> 07:27:56.051
Wellby: And we don't have to fight it at all. The holy water just kills it.

07:27:56.091 --> 07:27:56.231
Unknown: Yeah.

07:27:56.271 --> 07:27:56.411
Unknown: Yeah.

07:27:58.731 --> 07:27:59.491
Wellby: That's a good solution.

07:27:59.611 --> 07:27:59.631
Unknown: Yeah.

07:27:59.631 --> 07:28:00.371
Seeker: We could possibly do that.

07:28:00.391 --> 07:28:02.051
Delwath: Which is how do we destroy the scepter?

07:28:04.931 --> 07:28:05.851
Kenzo: I think the ladder does it.

07:28:06.291 --> 07:28:10.291
Wellby: I think the ladder does it. The ladder, the only one of us that died in battle.

07:28:10.291 --> 07:28:11.851
Seeker: [laughs] So true.

07:28:12.091 --> 07:28:14.431
Delwath: I mean, I guess the ladder could force punch it, right?

07:28:14.451 --> 07:28:15.791
Delwath: Like in theory.

07:28:15.791 --> 07:28:17.491
Delwath: Wait, I'll just grab, glass destroy it.

07:28:17.731 --> 07:28:19.451
Wellby: Wait, wait. Is there a way to do this-

07:28:19.751 --> 07:28:21.771
Unknown: Uh, it needs to be hit with something.

07:28:23.351 --> 07:28:24.711
DM: That's what we were told.

07:28:24.711 --> 07:28:26.411
Kenzo: Can the ladder hit it with itself?

07:28:28.171 --> 07:28:30.631
Kenzo: Can the ladder grapple it and just smash it, just like kinda-

07:28:30.871 --> 07:28:33.391
Delwath: You gotta hit it with the sword and then do...

07:28:33.391 --> 07:28:34.451
Delwath: The magic circle takes time.

07:28:34.471 --> 07:28:35.091
Delwath: Oh, no. Does it?

07:28:35.211 --> 07:28:36.711
DM: No. It's an action.

07:28:36.711 --> 07:28:37.591
DM: Just stab it.

07:28:38.711 --> 07:28:41.731
DM: You could hit it with the sword, and then as long as you don't lose initiative-

07:28:42.531 --> 07:28:43.871
Delwath: Yeah, that's a risky move

07:28:43.871 --> 07:28:47.071
DM: ... you can stab it, stab the sword in and then just run out.

07:28:52.931 --> 07:28:55.111
DM: Seeker can borrow inspiration from initiative.

07:28:55.131 --> 07:28:55.771
Kenzo: That's true.

07:28:55.811 --> 07:28:56.751
DM: Hello.

07:28:56.751 --> 07:28:58.110
Delwath: Still a bit of a risky move.

07:28:58.491 --> 07:29:05.791
Kenzo: That feels pretty fucking risky [laughs] for this, like, super powerful undead thing that then has an opportunity to cast spells at us.

07:29:05.791 --> 07:29:06.891
Delwath: I mean-

07:29:06.931 --> 07:29:07.211
Delwath: Like Tana-

07:29:07.231 --> 07:29:09.271
DM: I don't know why Kenzo's staff couldn't destroy it.

07:29:09.271 --> 07:29:09.771
Delwath: Oh, that's true.

07:29:09.811 --> 07:29:10.671
DM: It's super magical.

07:29:11.011 --> 07:29:14.651
Delwath: Yeah. Why don't you... Yes. You can, you can go in the magic circle.

07:29:15.011 --> 07:29:16.371
Kenzo: Oh, I love this plan. Okay.

07:29:16.391 --> 07:29:16.731
DM: Right?

07:29:17.591 --> 07:29:20.531
Delwath: Smash the thing and then just run out.

07:29:21.271 --> 07:29:22.491
Kenzo: Okay. Oh.

07:29:22.491 --> 07:29:23.671
DM: You just have to win initiative.

07:29:23.731 --> 07:29:29.211
DM: No, he doesn't because attacking the, attacking the object is an action.

07:29:29.211 --> 07:29:31.311
DM: He still has his move after the action finishes.

07:29:31.331 --> 07:29:31.331
Unknown: Ah, right.

07:29:31.331 --> 07:29:31.751
Delwath: The worst that can happen-

07:29:31.751 --> 07:29:32.731
Delwath: So you just smash and run

07:29:32.731 --> 07:29:34.331
DM: ... is he'd take an attack of opportunity.

07:29:34.371 --> 07:29:35.651
DM: Right. Okay.

07:29:35.651 --> 07:29:36.471
Kenzo: Fine. I'm down for that.

07:29:36.971 --> 07:29:37.891
Wellby: And then get grappled.

07:29:38.931 --> 07:29:39.011
Unknown: If-

07:29:39.091 --> 07:29:41.411
DM: I couldn't, like, grapple you with attack of opportunity.

07:29:41.431 --> 07:29:43.531
DM: That could be sort of nasty. No, but I'll cast Sanctuary.

07:29:45.951 --> 07:29:48.891
Kenzo: Wait, so this... Oh, you can also counterspell if it does something like that.

07:29:48.931 --> 07:29:49.671
Delwath: Yeah, if it casts a spell.

07:29:49.691 --> 07:29:50.651
Kenzo: We both can counterspell.

07:29:50.731 --> 07:29:50.851
Unknown: Yeah.

07:29:50.931 --> 07:29:52.111
Delwath: That's good, so we can go in and do anything.

07:29:52.151 --> 07:29:53.771
Delwath: But, but I could cast Sanctuary on you

07:29:54.831 --> 07:29:57.631
Delwath: 'cause then it can't, it won't be able to attack you.

07:29:58.711 --> 07:29:59.871
Delwath: Hm.

07:29:59.871 --> 07:30:00.091
Unknown: Right?

07:30:01.531 --> 07:30:04.571
Delwath: Then your Sanctuary, you go in, you smash.

07:30:04.571 --> 07:30:05.391
Kenzo: How long does Sanctuary last?

07:30:05.631 --> 07:30:07.031
Delwath: I don't know. I think it lasts a minute.

07:30:07.071 --> 07:30:08.171
DM: No, just it's a round.

07:30:08.451 --> 07:30:09.391
Delwath: Oh, it just lasts a round?

07:30:09.551 --> 07:30:12.691
DM: Oh, no. It lasts till you make an attack, but attacking the scepter would be an attack.

07:30:12.751 --> 07:30:15.851
Delwath: Does attacking the sep- that does not feel like it should count as an attack.

07:30:15.991 --> 07:30:17.851
DM: It's like an evil magical item.

07:30:17.971 --> 07:30:18.011
Unknown: Okay.

07:30:18.031 --> 07:30:18.551
Kenzo: I think that's an attack. That's fair.

07:30:18.551 --> 07:30:20.611
Delwath: Fair enough. It's an attack. No, no, fair enough.

07:30:20.611 --> 07:30:21.431
Delwath: Fair enough. Fair enough.

07:30:22.351 --> 07:30:23.631
Wellby: Is there any... Returning to Tane a second.

07:30:23.631 --> 07:30:24.911
Delwath: It lasts for a minute.

07:30:24.971 --> 07:30:27.971
Wellby: Is there any reason that not remembering

07:30:29.131 --> 07:30:33.971
Wellby: how the scepter is destroyed or that it's destroyed or anything like that is advantageous?

07:30:33.971 --> 07:30:35.831
Wellby: 'Cause that might shape how we go about doing it.

07:30:36.391 --> 07:30:36.571
Unknown: Hm.

07:30:36.571 --> 07:30:37.811
Wellby: But I don't know if it actually is.

07:30:37.911 --> 07:30:38.571
Kenzo: I don't think it does.

07:30:41.527 --> 07:30:44.447
Wellby: If our forgetting it removed Apollyon's forgetting of it,

07:30:45.547 --> 07:30:46.067
Wellby: that'd be good.

07:30:47.187 --> 07:30:50.787
Unknown: But, like, does us destroying the scepter now mean that Apollyon can't come back?

07:30:50.827 --> 07:30:51.367
Delwath: In theory.

07:30:52.927 --> 07:30:54.787
Unknown: Did we, like, kind of win the campaign if we do this right?

07:30:54.927 --> 07:30:57.187
Wellby: Does Apollyon know that we've destroyed the scepter?

07:30:57.607 --> 07:30:58.407
Kenzo: I'm sure it'll know.

07:30:59.467 --> 07:31:01.187
Delwath: None of us really know what happens.

07:31:01.687 --> 07:31:03.147
Seeker: He would just have to make another scepter.

07:31:03.147 --> 07:31:06.867
Seeker: He made the first one. He made this one in the first place.

07:31:06.867 --> 07:31:07.587
Seeker: Not unique

07:31:08.527 --> 07:31:10.247
Seeker: or like it's not like he, he-

07:31:10.287 --> 07:31:11.887
Unknown: I'm sure it was hard

07:31:11.887 --> 07:31:12.267
Seeker: ... right.

07:31:13.986 --> 07:31:16.947
Seeker: Also, our whole picture of what the scepter is and does,

07:31:18.407 --> 07:31:25.147
Seeker: and that it's got a fiend inside and everything is based on Amex's speculation and something a fae told us, so

07:31:26.727 --> 07:31:29.027
Unknown: could be partly wrong or incomplete.

07:31:29.027 --> 07:31:31.987
Unknown: I mean, or do we just use it one time before we-

07:31:32.187 --> 07:31:32.707
DM: Just one time

07:31:32.707 --> 07:31:34.047
Kenzo: ... I'm saying, you know, just to like-

07:31:34.127 --> 07:31:34.287
DM: One time

07:31:34.287 --> 07:31:36.247
Unknown: ... we have, the, just this whole fucking time-

07:31:36.367 --> 07:31:36.487
DM: Just-

07:31:36.487 --> 07:31:37.167
Kenzo: ... it's been like this

07:31:37.167 --> 07:31:37.767
DM: ... just to end part of it.

07:31:37.827 --> 07:31:39.027
Wellby: Is this Kenza saying this?

07:31:39.847 --> 07:31:39.907
DM: Yeah.

07:31:39.927 --> 07:31:40.087
Unknown: Okay.

07:31:40.247 --> 07:31:40.887
Wellby: There you go.

07:31:40.947 --> 07:31:41.647
Seeker: You know what I'm saying?

07:31:41.647 --> 07:31:42.727
DM: Just the tip of the scepter.

07:31:42.787 --> 07:31:43.467
Wellby: Just like this.

07:31:43.467 --> 07:31:44.407
Unknown: [laughs]

07:31:44.467 --> 07:31:45.947
DM: Just put it in a little bit.

07:31:45.947 --> 07:31:46.407
DM: [laughs]

07:31:46.487 --> 07:31:48.147
Unknown: Just a pinky, you know? Just a little.

07:31:48.887 --> 07:31:51.007
Unknown: Just, just, just a little bit corrupted by the...

07:31:51.027 --> 07:31:51.827
DM: Yeah. [laughs]

