08:08:01.905 --> 08:08:04.105
DM: Well, I assume you're asking what happened here, right?

08:08:04.105 --> 08:08:04.645
Delwath: Yeah.

08:08:04.645 --> 08:08:10.085
Delwath: Well, whoa, whoa, hold on, hold on. Do we wanna say what happened here or what happened to him?

08:08:12.065 --> 08:08:14.525
Unknown: I think it's what happened to him.

08:08:14.525 --> 08:08:15.425
Delwath: I think so, too.

08:08:16.185 --> 08:08:17.745
Delwath: Like, I wanna know was he, like,

08:08:19.345 --> 08:08:20.225
Delwath: corrupted?

08:08:21.525 --> 08:08:24.025
Delwath: Like, what caused him to be so evil,

08:08:25.045 --> 08:08:25.365
Seeker: right?

08:08:25.785 --> 08:08:25.985
Wellby: Yeah.

08:08:26.465 --> 08:08:28.645
Delwath: More than what happened right here, right now.

08:08:28.665 --> 08:08:30.545
Wellby: It's like what's the story of him coming here?

08:08:30.685 --> 08:08:30.765
Unknown: Yeah.

08:08:30.785 --> 08:08:32.265
Wellby: Or the helmet's journey.

08:08:32.585 --> 08:08:34.425
Delwath: The helmet's journey to this place.

08:08:34.625 --> 08:08:34.645
Wellby: The.

08:08:34.665 --> 08:08:34.885
Unknown: Yeah.

08:08:34.905 --> 08:08:35.385
Wellby: Time.

08:08:36.545 --> 08:08:37.685
Seeker: Well, he bought it last week.

08:08:37.925 --> 08:08:40.405
Wellby: I feel like the higher we roll, the more lenient the DM is.

08:08:40.405 --> 08:08:41.725
Unknown: [laughs]

08:08:41.725 --> 08:08:44.545
Wellby: So just do that military inspire.

08:08:44.585 --> 08:08:44.705
Unknown: Is that-

08:08:44.705 --> 08:08:45.105
Kenzo: Inspiration

08:08:45.105 --> 08:08:46.585
Seeker: ... inspiration.

08:08:46.625 --> 08:08:49.405
Seeker: D10. [dice rolling] Oh, motherfucker.

08:08:49.545 --> 08:08:50.585
Wellby: All right.

08:08:50.585 --> 08:08:51.665
Kenzo: Wait, did I get a plus what?

08:08:52.805 --> 08:08:53.165
DM: Plus

08:08:54.165 --> 08:08:54.665
DM: three?

08:08:54.665 --> 08:08:56.165
Delwath: What's your wisdom? Plus three.

08:08:56.165 --> 08:08:56.685
DM: Plus three.

08:08:57.265 --> 08:08:58.165
Kenzo: It's more than that, right?

08:08:58.845 --> 08:08:59.145
DM: No.

08:08:59.145 --> 08:09:02.785
Delwath: [dice rolling] Plus 10.

08:09:02.965 --> 08:09:03.365
Delwath: Fat house.

08:09:03.365 --> 08:09:04.225
DM: Hey, all right, 15.

08:09:04.325 --> 08:09:05.385
Kenzo: 15.

08:09:05.385 --> 08:09:05.585
DM: Okay.

08:09:07.705 --> 08:09:09.565
DM: So you show the helmet up to the mirror.

08:09:09.565 --> 08:09:10.905
Kenzo: Thanks for the inspiration.

08:09:10.905 --> 08:09:15.925
DM: [coughs] And, um, the first thing that you see is,

08:09:17.245 --> 08:09:20.845
DM: so like always, like the scene fades for a moment.

08:09:22.845 --> 08:09:24.385
DM: Um, and then you see,

08:09:26.145 --> 08:09:26.324
DM: uh,

08:09:27.485 --> 08:09:29.025
DM: the, uh,

08:09:30.565 --> 08:09:30.925
DM: so

08:09:32.405 --> 08:09:35.685
DM: standing on the bow of a ship. The ship, actually, you recognize the ship, right?

08:09:35.685 --> 08:09:37.005
DM: This is the ship that's docked.

08:09:37.465 --> 08:09:37.605
Unknown: Right.

08:09:37.625 --> 08:09:38.245
DM: At the docks.

08:09:38.785 --> 08:09:39.125
DM: Mm-hmm.

08:09:39.205 --> 08:09:39.345
DM: Um,

08:09:41.425 --> 08:09:42.385
DM: and, uh,

08:09:46.365 --> 08:09:52.145
DM: uh, Urgall, presumably, whoever's wearing the helmet, um, is standing

08:09:53.805 --> 08:09:55.065
DM: in front of a,

08:09:56.265 --> 08:09:56.445
DM: uh,

08:09:58.765 --> 08:10:02.565
DM: so- some sort of, um, merchant, trader.

08:10:02.565 --> 08:10:05.805
DM: Like, somebody, um, dressed in nice clothes.

08:10:06.325 --> 08:10:12.065
DM: Uh, but being, like, held up by the neck and, like, who's, like, shouting something

08:10:13.025 --> 08:10:14.885
DM: at, at Urgall.

08:10:14.885 --> 08:10:15.245
Delwath: Does the-

08:10:15.325 --> 08:10:16.825
Seeker: Urgall's the one being held up in the air?

08:10:16.885 --> 08:10:17.605
DM: No, no, no.

08:10:17.625 --> 08:10:18.005
Kenzo: It's a trade.

08:10:18.005 --> 08:10:19.485
