08:36:15.761 --> 08:36:16.581
DM: with the moon in the...

08:36:17.361 --> 08:36:18.561
DM: rising in the right position-

08:36:18.601 --> 08:36:20.241
Wellby: Oh, shit. Right. That's what we were waiting for.

08:36:20.541 --> 08:36:21.201
Seeker: Yeah. [laughs]

08:36:21.241 --> 08:36:24.321
Seeker: Oh, we have something to do. Is the, uh, is the thing on?

08:36:24.401 --> 08:36:24.581
Wellby: Yeah.

08:36:25.201 --> 08:36:26.761
Unknown: You wanna put some... Do we have some good, uh-

08:36:26.781 --> 08:36:27.341
Wellby: Yeah, I wanna put some-

08:36:27.341 --> 08:36:28.201
Delwath: ... summoning demons in?

08:36:28.221 --> 08:36:30.661
Kenzo: This is, this is the big climax 'cause I think the campaign's over after this.

08:36:32.081 --> 08:36:32.361
DM: Uh,

08:36:33.261 --> 08:36:40.061
DM: just 'cause, like, Apollyon can't, like, you know, materialize as a god doesn't mean he's weak.

08:36:40.461 --> 08:36:41.641
Delwath: Right. I, I think-

08:36:41.681 --> 08:36:44.281
Unknown: We still have a campaign. We still have, we still have a climactic battle worth of campaign.

08:36:44.321 --> 08:36:49.221
Delwath: I, I think, I think it's just that Talgar can no longer be destroyed by Apollyon.

08:36:50.121 --> 08:36:51.201
Delwath: He can still kill us.

08:36:51.201 --> 08:36:55.121
DM: The reason Apollyon wanted the three items was to become a god.

08:36:55.681 --> 08:36:56.281
Wellby: Right.

08:36:56.281 --> 08:36:58.341
DM: That was his whole goal. He wanted to turn himself-

08:36:58.361 --> 08:36:58.441
Unknown: I mean-

08:36:58.441 --> 08:36:59.641
DM: ... into the god of the humans.

08:36:59.661 --> 08:36:59.921
Wellby: Right.

08:36:59.921 --> 08:37:01.881
DM: Like, the firstborn of the humans, basically.

08:37:01.961 --> 08:37:02.061
Wellby: Right.

08:37:02.061 --> 08:37:02.961
DM: Well, the firstborn of the-

08:37:03.741 --> 08:37:03.881
Unknown: Drink wine

08:37:03.881 --> 08:37:04.481
DM: ... of the good humans.

08:37:04.561 --> 08:37:05.061
Wellby: Oh, yeah.

08:37:05.061 --> 08:37:05.421
DM: The pure humans.

08:37:05.441 --> 08:37:06.401
Wellby: Human supremacy.

08:37:06.481 --> 08:37:06.661
Unknown: Yeah.

08:37:06.701 --> 08:37:07.361
Wellby: Right. Yeah.

08:37:07.381 --> 08:37:11.681
Delwath: I mean, we could maybe just, now that he can't actually become a god, wander off.

08:37:12.901 --> 08:37:13.601
DM: We could.

08:37:13.761 --> 08:37:15.401
Unknown: I, I, I think at this point, you know-

08:37:15.441 --> 08:37:16.161
Seeker: But maybe he'll be-

08:37:16.161 --> 08:37:16.841
Wellby: ... if we go back, he just-

08:37:16.841 --> 08:37:20.301
DM: ... super pissed at you that you kept him from being a god

08:37:20.341 --> 08:37:21.801
Delwath: It... He... It's true.

08:37:21.801 --> 08:37:23.081
Delwath: He might get mad at us.

08:37:23.741 --> 08:37:26.901
Wellby: I, I feel like from Wub's perspective, like, the next priority,

08:37:27.841 --> 08:37:30.101
Wellby: if Apollyon is stopped, is vengeance.

08:37:30.461 --> 08:37:30.841
Seeker: Vengeance.

08:37:31.121 --> 08:37:31.301
Unknown: Oh, uh, yeah.

08:37:31.321 --> 08:37:32.261
Wellby: Like, revenge on Grash-

08:37:32.301 --> 08:37:32.501
Unknown: Yeah. Yeah

08:37:32.501 --> 08:37:33.581
Wellby: ... revenge on Fausto.

08:37:33.641 --> 08:37:34.641
Delwath: Fausto.

08:37:34.641 --> 08:37:34.781
Wellby: Like-

08:37:35.201 --> 08:37:36.141
Delwath: Really-

08:37:36.141 --> 08:37:37.621
Wellby: ... tie up those loose threads

08:37:37.621 --> 08:37:38.981
Delwath: ... needs his...

08:37:39.121 --> 08:37:40.281
Seeker: Or we just live large

08:37:40.969 --> 08:37:42.349
Delwath: But what better way to wage large than-

08:37:42.349 --> 08:37:44.089
Wellby: I think we can move large while they're still out there

08:37:44.089 --> 08:37:46.189
Delwath: ... kill Fausto and take all his stuff?

08:37:46.669 --> 08:37:49.809
Wellby: Tower in Chardin? Giant tower drops the airship.

08:37:49.809 --> 08:37:51.249
Delwath: Giant tower... Talk to the... I... Yes.

08:37:51.609 --> 08:37:52.089
Kenzo: True that. True that.

08:37:52.129 --> 08:37:52.369
Unknown: Or-

08:37:52.549 --> 08:37:54.009
Kenzo: Fausto is next. Fausto's next

08:37:54.009 --> 08:37:59.929
Delwath: ... you could probably sell... I mean, I don't know how we get title to his tower, but, like, you could also sell it-

08:38:00.089 --> 08:38:00.669
DM: Okay, so-

08:38:00.669 --> 08:38:01.189
Delwath: ... for quite a bit

08:38:01.189 --> 08:38:02.129
DM: ... you go-

08:38:02.449 --> 08:38:04.089
Wellby: It's the perfect dock for the boat, though

08:38:04.089 --> 08:38:04.289
Unknown: ... draw-

08:38:04.309 --> 08:38:05.589
Delwath: But I don't wanna live in Chardin.

08:38:06.529 --> 08:38:08.429
Wellby: No, it's just, it's, it's like our summer house.

08:38:08.429 --> 08:38:10.329
Unknown: [laughs]

08:38:10.329 --> 08:38:10.809
Wellby: You're saying.

08:38:11.869 --> 08:38:15.049
DM: You return to the sacred waters and take the scepter out.

08:38:15.609 --> 08:38:17.369
DM: Who's taking... Is Wellby taking the scepter out?

08:38:19.009 --> 08:38:25.769
Wellby: Wellby is taking the scepter out and he is, he is, like, putting down everything else.

08:38:25.769 --> 08:38:27.169
Wellby: Like, he is just in,

08:38:28.589 --> 08:38:31.709
Wellby: like, pants and a shirt and none of his other stuff.

08:38:32.709 --> 08:38:34.069
Wellby: Like, I, I don't have a lot of-

08:38:34.789 --> 08:38:35.609
Seeker: Where, where are we putting-

08:38:35.609 --> 08:38:36.029
Wellby: ... for us

08:38:36.029 --> 08:38:38.629
Seeker: ... the portable hole temporarily?

08:38:38.629 --> 08:38:39.629
Seeker: Uh, the scepter.

08:38:39.649 --> 08:38:40.089
DM: The scepter.

08:38:40.669 --> 08:38:42.569
Unknown: Wow, how did you do that? That's cool.

08:38:43.329 --> 08:38:44.289
Kenzo: Wow.

08:38:45.389 --> 08:38:46.489
Wellby: So takes it out.

08:38:50.149 --> 08:38:50.789
Seeker: Oh, man.

08:38:52.709 --> 08:38:53.669
Seeker: It was a good scepter.

08:38:56.389 --> 08:38:56.869
Kenzo: Don't do it.

08:38:57.229 --> 08:38:59.569
Wellby: It's not too late to do something differently with this.

08:39:00.329 --> 08:39:01.209
Seeker: Don't do it, Wellby.

08:39:01.229 --> 08:39:01.889
Seeker: Are, are you gonna-

08:39:03.029 --> 08:39:04.389
Kenzo: Don't do it

08:39:04.389 --> 08:39:05.869
Seeker: ... s- command the rest of us?

08:39:06.769 --> 08:39:07.389
Wellby: No, but I mean-

08:39:07.489 --> 08:39:07.489
Unknown: To act

08:39:07.489 --> 08:39:09.849
Wellby: ... what if all of us together attune to it?

08:39:11.549 --> 08:39:12.889
Delwath: Del is pointed at the water.

08:39:13.949 --> 08:39:14.989
Delwath: Go quicker, Wellby.

08:39:15.569 --> 08:39:17.149
Wellby: Mm. Mm, mm.

08:39:19.969 --> 08:39:20.529
Kenzo: Drop it.

08:39:22.489 --> 08:39:22.829
Wellby: Yeah.

08:39:23.789 --> 08:39:24.929
Wellby: All right. Fuck, fine.

08:39:27.109 --> 08:39:27.529
Wellby: Out it goes.

08:39:27.869 --> 08:39:30.449
DM: You release the scepter and it falls,

08:39:31.469 --> 08:39:32.649
DM: sinks below the water.

08:39:33.969 --> 08:39:35.149
Wellby: Now we wait.

08:39:35.789 --> 08:39:36.549
Delwath: And you wait.

08:39:38.409 --> 08:39:39.229
Seeker: Does anything happen to it?

08:39:39.889 --> 08:39:40.549
Delwath: We have to wait a day.

08:39:41.449 --> 08:39:42.129
Delwath: 24 hours.

08:39:43.709 --> 08:39:45.269
Kenzo: For the fiend to loosen its grip.

08:39:45.349 --> 08:39:46.969
DM: You, you set and you wait.

08:39:47.489 --> 08:39:47.869
Kenzo: Tim, while all-

08:39:47.949 --> 08:39:50.669
Delwath: Del was gonna stand guard, like, sword drawn.

08:39:50.688 --> 08:39:51.049
Kenzo: Oh, yeah. Yeah, whatever

08:39:51.049 --> 08:39:52.189
Delwath: ... standing in the water,

08:39:53.709 --> 08:39:55.709
Delwath: like on the edge of the water, like a watch-

08:39:55.729 --> 08:39:56.989
Wellby: What, like next to the scepter?

08:39:57.029 --> 08:39:57.229
Unknown: Yes.

08:39:57.289 --> 08:39:58.549
Delwath: Uh, like 10 feet away.

08:39:58.709 --> 08:39:59.029
Kenzo: Actually, yeah

08:39:59.029 --> 08:39:59.429
Kenzo: ... 15 feet away.

08:39:59.869 --> 08:40:01.349
Wellby: All right. Wellby's suit back up again.

08:40:02.129 --> 08:40:02.789
Seeker: Tim, this, uh, this whole, uh-

08:40:02.829 --> 08:40:04.349
Wellby: And stand guard over Del.

08:40:04.349 --> 08:40:05.509
Wellby: [laughs]

08:40:05.509 --> 08:40:09.309
Kenzo: [laughs] Kenzo spent a lot of time vibing in this water for the past, like, two days.

08:40:09.909 --> 08:40:09.929
Unknown: Mm-hmm.

08:40:09.929 --> 08:40:11.949
Kenzo: What, what's, what's going on now that the scepter's in there?

08:40:11.969 --> 08:40:13.849
Kenzo: Like, what, how does, what's, what's the energy of the water like?

08:40:14.209 --> 08:40:14.609
DM: Um-

08:40:14.629 --> 08:40:15.209
Kenzo: The sacred waters

08:40:15.209 --> 08:40:20.309
DM: ... the, the sacred waters seem unbothered by the presence of the sector, scepter.

08:40:20.369 --> 08:40:21.269
Kenzo: Interesting.

08:40:21.369 --> 08:40:26.789
DM: I, I mean, this m- magic is older and deeper than the magic of fiends.

08:40:26.969 --> 08:40:27.309
Wellby: Sure.

08:40:27.869 --> 08:40:28.469
Wellby: Hmm.

08:40:28.469 --> 08:40:29.409
DM: But the scepter,

08:40:32.989 --> 08:40:34.629
DM: a- as you stand guard...

08:40:34.629 --> 08:40:41.609
Wellby: [laughs] I feel like it's less of guard and more of a standoff

08:40:41.609 --> 08:40:42.929
Kenzo: ... magic circle? Magic circle?

08:40:42.929 --> 08:40:43.109
Unknown: Magic circle?

08:40:43.189 --> 08:40:44.429
DM: No, you got, you got to save it.

08:40:44.429 --> 08:40:45.429
Kenzo: I mean, you're, you're-

08:40:45.489 --> 08:40:47.949
Delwath: I gotta s- I, I gotta save it for the fiend.

08:40:48.469 --> 08:40:48.669
Unknown: Right.

08:40:49.129 --> 08:40:51.509
Delwath: If the f- doesn't, the fiend doesn't come out till we break the scepter.

08:40:52.029 --> 08:40:53.929
Kenzo: Right. But okay, well, what's happening to the scepter?

08:40:53.929 --> 08:40:54.569
Kenzo: We think.

08:40:54.629 --> 08:40:55.129
Kenzo: Yeah, we think.

08:40:56.409 --> 08:40:57.249
Delwath: I might, I mean-

08:40:57.389 --> 08:40:59.069
Wellby: It's just, it's just right there

08:40:59.069 --> 08:41:00.409
DM: ... it's sitting there.

08:41:00.409 --> 08:41:04.469
DM: Like, anybody could reach down and pick it up.

08:41:04.469 --> 08:41:05.429
Unknown: [laughs]

08:41:06.629 --> 08:41:08.149
Kenzo: No, no. Is there anybody...

08:41:08.149 --> 08:41:10.489
Unknown: Wait, hold on, hold on. Is there anybody in the r- around?

08:41:10.829 --> 08:41:11.829
DM: Just the four of you.

08:41:11.829 --> 08:41:17.809
Wellby: [laughs] I definitely have this vision of the four of us each just standing like 10 feet apart.

08:41:18.569 --> 08:41:18.769
Unknown: Like staring.

08:41:18.769 --> 08:41:20.169
Wellby: Like looking back and forth.

08:41:20.389 --> 08:41:22.589
Delwath: I mean, Delath, like, has his sword drawn, right?

08:41:22.589 --> 08:41:27.869
Delwath: Like, not at, facing you guys, but, like, watching the scepter and watching the area.

08:41:28.729 --> 08:41:30.029
Seeker: When you look at Seeker-

08:41:30.089 --> 08:41:30.489
Wellby: It's your battle stance

08:41:30.489 --> 08:41:33.309
Seeker: ... and then look away, and then look at Seeker again, you, you may notice-

08:41:33.349 --> 08:41:33.629
Kenzo: While he looks-

08:41:33.629 --> 08:41:34.949
Seeker: ... that he's gotten an inch closer

08:41:34.949 --> 08:41:36.809
Delwath: ... he looks over at you occasionally.

08:41:37.909 --> 08:41:38.889
Delwath: Delath does, I mean.

08:41:40.449 --> 08:41:45.309
Kenzo: Kenzo closes his eyes and s- sits, and sits in the, uh, sits down in the water and is just, is just meditating.

08:41:46.209 --> 08:41:48.989
Seeker: There's a slight keening sound coming from Seeker's direction.

08:41:48.989 --> 08:41:49.569
Wellby: Yeah, that, that's preparation for battle.

08:41:51.909 --> 08:41:53.769
DM: An hour passes, two.

08:41:55.889 --> 08:41:59.689
Kenzo: Three. Is anything happening to the scepter? Is it, like, bubbling or, like, shaking or just sitting there?

08:41:59.989 --> 08:42:01.389
Seeker: It's just sitting in the water.

08:42:01.429 --> 08:42:03.529
DM: The sun rises higher in the sky.

08:42:03.529 --> 08:42:07.169
DM: The glow, bronze glow of the ceiling lights.

08:42:07.949 --> 08:42:08.229
Wellby: Um...

08:42:11.209 --> 08:42:13.409
Seeker: May- maybe we should take it out again and see how it's doing.

08:42:16.149 --> 08:42:16.529
Wellby: I don't think-

08:42:16.569 --> 08:42:16.609
Unknown: It's okay

08:42:16.609 --> 08:42:18.869
Wellby: ... I don't think that's a good... I think it has to stay under there for-

08:42:19.069 --> 08:42:19.449
Delwath: It does

08:42:19.449 --> 08:42:20.309
Wellby: ... for 24 hours.

08:42:20.309 --> 08:42:23.089
Seeker: It's gotta, it's gotta stay under. It's gotta stay under.

08:42:23.089 --> 08:42:24.589
DM: Another hour passes.

08:42:25.069 --> 08:42:26.269
DM: Seems like five.

08:42:26.589 --> 08:42:27.629
Kenzo: You can try the music a little, Tim.

08:42:27.689 --> 08:42:28.849
Wellby: And we don't hear it at all?

08:42:29.289 --> 08:42:30.149
DM: You don't hear anything.

08:42:34.109 --> 08:42:35.349
DM: Another hour passes.

08:42:35.349 --> 08:42:37.149
DM: The sun barely reaches

08:42:39.089 --> 08:42:39.289
Unknown: the top.

08:42:39.309 --> 08:42:43.569
Wellby: Does it still have detect magic? We didn't, like, fuck up and get the scepter swapped out on us somehow, did we?

08:42:45.289 --> 08:42:46.609
Delwath: I can... Yeah, I'll, I'll...

08:42:47.789 --> 08:42:49.069
Delwath: It's magical, I assume.

08:42:49.329 --> 08:42:49.849
DM: Yep.

08:42:49.849 --> 08:42:50.269
Wellby: All right.

08:42:50.749 --> 08:42:51.769
Kenzo: It's the scepter.

08:42:51.769 --> 08:42:52.149
Wellby: All right.

08:42:52.169 --> 08:42:54.029
Kenzo: This is real. We're, we're doing the right things.

08:42:54.029 --> 08:42:55.229
Seeker: Everything's good.

08:42:55.229 --> 08:42:56.589
Seeker: Not some kind of fake scepter.

08:42:56.609 --> 08:43:01.149
DM: The sun passes noon and begins to sink again in the sky.

08:43:04.629 --> 08:43:05.069
DM: See

08:43:08.269 --> 08:43:10.929
DM: not exactly images in the water,

08:43:12.169 --> 08:43:12.789
DM: just little

08:43:14.109 --> 08:43:15.289
DM: hints like,

08:43:17.729 --> 08:43:19.249
DM: what if you had this power?

08:43:20.329 --> 08:43:22.549
Unknown: What would you see? What would you do?

08:43:24.489 --> 08:43:28.769
DM: Drifting across the water, drifting closer to the scepter.

08:43:30.769 --> 08:43:30.969
Unknown: Ah.

08:43:33.869 --> 08:43:35.369
DM: Another hour passes.

08:43:36.769 --> 08:43:38.189
DM: Another hour.

08:43:38.189 --> 08:43:40.389
DM: Begins to get dark. The sun sets.

08:43:40.629 --> 08:43:41.409
Kenzo: How many hours has it been now?

08:43:42.509 --> 08:43:43.349
DM: Like seven.

08:43:45.609 --> 08:43:46.689
Seeker: Seeker's toes are in the water

08:43:49.693 --> 08:43:53.333
Seeker: He, he seems to jolt awake and realize this and then pull them out again

08:43:56.053 --> 08:43:56.853
DM: It gets dark.

08:43:58.853 --> 08:44:01.293
DM: Although you don't fully notice it in the

08:44:02.753 --> 08:44:11.073
DM: inside, it's just the light from the open door fades, turns red at the glow of sunset and then to darkness.

08:44:11.073 --> 08:44:13.573
Unknown: [laughs]

08:44:13.573 --> 08:44:13.673
Wellby: Mm.

08:44:13.673 --> 08:44:16.093
Unknown: But you can, you can feel the moon.

08:44:17.173 --> 08:44:24.253
DM: You can feel the pull on the water, 'cause the moon controls the extra planar tides.

08:44:25.433 --> 08:44:28.953
DM: When the moon is full, the outer planes are closer.

08:44:30.233 --> 08:44:31.433
Seeker: It's a were-scepter.

08:44:34.593 --> 08:44:36.413
DM: Another hour passes, two,

08:44:38.073 --> 08:44:38.633
DM: three.

08:44:40.753 --> 08:44:41.953
DM: It's approaching dinner time.

08:44:41.953 --> 08:44:43.153
DM: You're all hungry.

08:44:44.413 --> 08:44:47.133
Seeker: When the moon is full, the outer planes are closer.

08:44:47.133 --> 08:44:48.233
Wellby: Kind of, Kenzo fasts.

08:44:48.973 --> 08:44:50.713
Unknown: Yeah, Delwath's gonna fast too, I think.

08:44:51.513 --> 08:44:53.033
Delwath: It doesn't feel like the right time to eat.

08:44:53.773 --> 08:44:54.113
Wellby: Yeah.

08:44:55.733 --> 08:44:56.353
Seeker: Seeker will eat.

08:44:56.353 --> 08:45:00.853
DM: [laughs] Anything to take his mind off the scepter.

08:45:01.373 --> 08:45:01.953
Seeker: He's just like

08:45:03.273 --> 08:45:07.973
Seeker: sort of like zombie-like munching on something, just staring at the scepter unmoving.

08:45:07.973 --> 08:45:09.533
DM: It gets to midnight,

08:45:11.173 --> 08:45:12.373
DM: darkest hour.

08:45:14.353 --> 08:45:21.353
DM: In the corner of o- your eye, you all like turn and think you see shadows skittering across the,

08:45:22.993 --> 08:45:25.253
DM: the water, skittering in the darkness.

08:45:25.253 --> 08:45:26.893
DM: All the shadows you fought, the

08:45:28.253 --> 08:45:31.493
DM: shadows that Grosh sent after you, the shadows that killed the,

08:45:32.613 --> 08:45:40.153
DM: um, the acolytes of the Mystai of, of Shakun when you were attacked during the initiation.

08:45:42.113 --> 08:45:46.213
DM: The shadows that hunted you outside of Chardin and nearly killed-

08:45:47.813 --> 08:45:48.273
Wellby: Kenzo.

08:45:48.793 --> 08:45:50.233
DM: No, the first time they...

08:45:50.233 --> 08:45:52.273
DM: No, Seeker did go down once before.

08:45:52.293 --> 08:45:52.333
Wellby: Mm.

08:45:52.333 --> 08:45:55.473
DM: That first shadow fight last summer on the Cape.

08:45:55.593 --> 08:45:55.853
DM: Mm.

08:45:55.853 --> 08:45:57.872
DM: They almost got away with Seeker.

08:45:59.893 --> 08:46:02.073
DM: The shadows that almost got away with Kenzo.

08:46:03.333 --> 08:46:13.913
DM: The sense that there's more, many more of them out hunting you somewhere in the world, and if you just reached down and picked up the scepter, they'd be yours to command.

08:46:13.933 --> 08:46:13.973
DM: And-

08:46:13.973 --> 08:46:15.493
Kenzo: What color is my sword?

08:46:15.493 --> 08:46:16.173
Delwath: Is it glowing at all?

08:46:17.233 --> 08:46:17.393
DM: Nope.

08:46:18.793 --> 08:46:21.993
DM: They'd be yours to command and not Fausto's to command.

08:46:21.993 --> 08:46:26.613
DM: You could send them after Fausto, and the shadows could

08:46:28.113 --> 08:46:28.853
DM: catch him.

08:46:29.813 --> 08:46:31.433
DM: You wouldn't even have to go to Chardin.

08:46:32.113 --> 08:46:37.353
DM: Vengeance could be yours if you just reach down and grab the scepter.

08:46:41.053 --> 08:46:42.413
DM: Another hour passes.

08:46:45.893 --> 08:46:47.573
DM: You can feel dawn is approaching,

08:46:48.993 --> 08:46:54.393
DM: but the shadows are gathered thick now in the room, like the light seems to dim.

08:46:57.753 --> 08:46:57.993
DM: The

08:47:00.833 --> 08:47:02.513
DM: flames that light up the,

08:47:03.773 --> 08:47:04.653
DM: uh, the,

08:47:06.433 --> 08:47:14.473
DM: the cast off the flickering roof, the bronze roof now rather than gold are a sort of pale, sickly yellow.

08:47:17.613 --> 08:47:19.193
DM: Dawn is an hour away.

08:47:21.813 --> 08:47:24.633
DM: Everybody is standing just tense, locked and

08:47:25.673 --> 08:47:26.653
DM: looking at each other.

08:47:27.533 --> 08:47:29.313
Kenzo: Kenzo's got his eyes closed, meditating.

08:47:30.273 --> 08:47:31.253
Seeker: Seeker's eating snacks.

08:47:32.553 --> 08:47:33.893
Wellby: Excuse, excuse Seeker, what?

08:47:34.813 --> 08:47:35.453
Seeker: Eating snacks.

08:47:36.053 --> 08:47:36.913
DM: That's Wellby, right?

08:47:37.573 --> 08:47:43.013
Wellby: Wellby has a sort of extraordinary relaxation that you know signals extreme anxiety and tension.

08:47:43.873 --> 08:47:44.813
DM: That's Delwath there, right?

08:47:45.253 --> 08:47:46.913
Delwath: He's still standing.

08:47:46.913 --> 08:47:49.633
Delwath: Um, his, uh, the,

08:47:51.233 --> 08:47:56.693
Delwath: um, [smacks lips] lynx has come off his shield and is pacing in a circle around the scepter.

08:47:58.793 --> 08:47:59.813
DM: Another hour passes.

08:47:59.813 --> 08:48:04.273
Delwath: And Delwath sort of keeps glancing over at it and then back at the door.

08:48:05.473 --> 08:48:08.952
Wellby: I'm just gonna step outside and just take a look around outside.

08:48:10.233 --> 08:48:18.493
DM: It's pre-dawn, like the, just before the sun rises, probably like 23 hours after you put the scepter in.

08:48:18.493 --> 08:48:20.873
Unknown: Nothing moving on the island.

08:48:21.893 --> 08:48:28.173
DM: The ocean, the weather, the waves, everything is dead still, quite unusually so for

08:48:29.573 --> 08:48:33.413
DM: midwinter. Like, normally there's more winds at this time of year.

08:48:33.413 --> 08:48:36.453
DM: The ocean is flat calm as far as you can see.

08:48:36.453 --> 08:48:37.533
Seeker: The goddess is appeased.

08:48:40.653 --> 08:48:40.853
Wellby: Mm.

08:48:43.493 --> 08:48:47.033
DM: Kenzo, you notice it first in your meditation.

08:48:49.073 --> 08:48:49.253
DM: A,

08:48:52.793 --> 08:49:02.353
DM: a light that's not a light, that's like a, a sensation of the deepest parts of the ocean, like the, the inverse of light.

08:49:02.873 --> 08:49:07.113
DM: The, but not an unpleasant darkness, the darkness of,

08:49:08.353 --> 08:49:12.593
DM: of the depth, the darkness of the weight of water above you-

08:49:13.213 --> 08:49:13.293
Wellby: Mm

08:49:13.293 --> 08:49:13.293
DM: ...

08:49:15.033 --> 08:49:17.113
DM: pressing down on the scepter.

08:49:20.913 --> 08:49:22.653
DM: Delwath, your sword begins to glow.

08:49:23.613 --> 08:49:24.293
Delwath: What does that mean again?

08:49:24.813 --> 08:49:27.793
Kenzo: It just means that there's a fiend nearby.

08:49:30.433 --> 08:49:30.993
Delwath: I'll, um,

08:49:31.833 --> 08:49:35.113
Delwath: I'll quietly call out to Kenzo that it's almost time.

08:49:36.713 --> 08:49:37.533
Wellby: Kenzo nods.

08:49:38.853 --> 08:49:45.653
DM: The weight of the ocean is getting heavier and heavier, and now you all can feel it, this

08:49:47.513 --> 08:49:51.233
DM: oppressive power.

08:49:51.233 --> 08:49:52.253
DM: It reminds you of,

08:49:53.373 --> 08:49:58.013
DM: Wellby, of like the worst storms that you survived as a child.

08:49:58.013 --> 08:50:07.593
DM: Like just clinging to the deck of the ship, ropes tied around you so that each wave that crashes across the bow doesn't wash you out to sea.

08:50:08.993 --> 08:50:09.233
Unknown: Mm.

08:50:13.873 --> 08:50:16.073
DM: Then you hear a crack

08:50:17.653 --> 08:50:20.313
DM: and this otherworldly screech,

08:50:22.233 --> 08:50:23.273
DM: and this sort of

08:50:26.693 --> 08:50:32.133
DM: sound like a thousand waves crashing at once, but really low, like the rumbling.

08:50:32.153 --> 08:50:40.413
DM: Like it's almost more like the sort of rumbling noise that rocks make when the wave rolls up the beach and then rolls out if like...

08:50:41.493 --> 08:50:45.373
DM: But just very low, almost below the limits of hearing.

08:50:50.573 --> 08:50:52.053
DM: It's been 24 hours.

08:50:54.273 --> 08:50:56.132
DM: Your sword is glowing brightly now.

08:50:57.753 --> 08:50:59.153
Kenzo: Kenzo stands up.

08:50:59.153 --> 08:51:01.153
Delwath: I'm gonna plant my sword next to the scepter.

08:51:01.733 --> 08:51:02.033
DM: Okay.

08:51:03.013 --> 08:51:05.933
DM: A magic circle springs up around the scepter.

08:51:07.073 --> 08:51:07.933
Kenzo: Seeker backs up.

08:51:11.293 --> 08:51:14.113
Kenzo: Kenzo takes this long, slow breaths.

08:51:15.753 --> 08:51:16.413
Kenzo: Each breath

08:51:17.953 --> 08:51:20.073
Kenzo: tuning in the energy of the sacred waters.

08:51:20.953 --> 08:51:21.573
Kenzo: Each breath

08:51:24.113 --> 08:51:26.353
Kenzo: giving a prayer. What's the name of, um...

08:51:26.353 --> 08:51:26.653
Kenzo: Kaikkea.

08:51:26.673 --> 08:51:30.053
Kenzo: Yeah.

08:51:30.053 --> 08:51:33.493
Kenzo: Going through the ritual prayer that he's learned from, um, the priestess,

08:51:34.513 --> 08:51:36.953
Kenzo: and that he's just been totally, um,

08:51:38.553 --> 08:51:41.553
Kenzo: attuned to over the past, uh, several days here.

08:51:44.713 --> 08:51:45.333
Kenzo: Each breath

08:51:48.213 --> 08:51:48.633
DM: slow,

08:51:49.553 --> 08:51:51.313
Kenzo: slow, focusing his power.

08:51:55.413 --> 08:51:56.213
Kenzo: After a moment...

08:51:57.113 --> 08:51:57.973
Kenzo: What time of day is it right now?

08:51:58.733 --> 08:51:59.013
DM: Dawn.

08:51:59.013 --> 08:51:59.893
Kenzo: Just after dawn.

08:51:59.893 --> 08:52:00.813
DM: Just after dawn.

08:52:01.613 --> 08:52:03.633
Kenzo: Perfect.

08:52:03.633 --> 08:52:05.373
Kenzo: What's the lighting in the room?

08:52:05.373 --> 08:52:15.373
DM: The, so it's these continual flame fires that are casting flickering fire light off the bronze roof, which for a while felt like

08:52:15.373 --> 08:52:19.813
DM: sickly yellow, but now is like flared like the, like the morning sun.

08:52:20.693 --> 08:52:22.253
DM: S- feels like sunrise.

08:52:22.493 --> 08:52:31.553
Wellby: What's like the image or memory that comes to mind or that you call to mind to like center in that moment for like what's about to come?

08:52:38.933 --> 08:52:39.113
Kenzo: Hmm.

08:52:42.293 --> 08:52:43.033
Kenzo: I think it's...

08:52:48.673 --> 08:52:49.373
Kenzo: Well, right now

08:52:54.013 --> 08:52:55.573
Unknown: we're about to unbind this thing.

08:53:05.673 --> 08:53:07.393
Unknown: I think it's, I think it's, um...

08:53:12.333 --> 08:53:14.193
Unknown: I think it's focusing on the moment

08:53:15.293 --> 08:53:15.393
Kenzo: of,

08:53:18.853 --> 08:53:19.133
Kenzo: like,

08:53:20.973 --> 08:53:22.413
Kenzo: destruction and creation.

08:53:23.693 --> 08:53:25.093
Kenzo: It's like that

08:53:27.173 --> 08:53:28.133
Kenzo: molecular edge-

08:53:28.473 --> 08:53:28.573
Unknown: Mm

08:53:28.573 --> 08:53:31.613
Unknown: ... between those two, those two states.

08:53:38.573 --> 08:53:40.473
Kenzo: And Kenzo imagines that line

08:53:41.993 --> 08:53:46.313
Kenzo: between imagi- between, between creation and, uh, destruction

08:53:49.133 --> 08:53:50.853
Kenzo: cutting right through the center of the scepter.

08:53:52.113 --> 08:53:53.213
Kenzo: And then with one

08:53:54.373 --> 08:53:55.073
Kenzo: solid swing,

08:53:56.393 --> 08:53:57.313
Kenzo: bring the staff down

08:53:58.653 --> 08:53:59.593
Kenzo: with all of his force.

08:54:01.713 --> 08:54:03.173
DM: As you raise the staff,

08:54:04.193 --> 08:54:10.213
DM: the waters draw back, like the ocean peeling back before a tsunami.

08:54:10.213 --> 08:54:20.513
DM: And as you bring your staff up to swing, the wa- the, the liquid of the sacred waters flows up along the top of your staff, and as you swing it down,

08:54:20.513 --> 08:54:25.073
DM: it's with the weight of the entire Green Sea behind your staff.

08:54:25.093 --> 08:54:25.113
Unknown: Whoa.

08:54:25.113 --> 08:54:30.033
DM: It feels like you're holding, feels like you're holding thousands of pounds of water.

08:54:30.413 --> 08:54:31.573
Delwath: Oh.

08:54:31.573 --> 08:54:32.033
Kenzo: Nice.

08:54:32.073 --> 08:54:42.313
DM: And it [imitates exploding sound] s- hits right in the center of the ha- the scepter and you see cracks start to form and race along

08:54:42.313 --> 08:54:47.913
DM: the two edges, and the scepter just begins to sort of slowly disintegrate from the center as you strike it.

08:54:49.933 --> 08:54:51.473
DM: And you run

08:54:52.493 --> 08:54:57.293
DM: out of the magic circle as there is this howling screech.

08:54:58.973 --> 08:55:01.473
DM: And what you see forming is not,

08:55:03.093 --> 08:55:07.333
DM: it's not a demon, or it's not a complete demon.

08:55:07.333 --> 08:55:08.933
DM: It's ragged.

08:55:08.933 --> 08:55:16.833
DM: It's like, it's like a sheet that's been ripped and shredded, and there's just a few like fragments of the sheet left.

08:55:16.853 --> 08:55:17.733
Delwath: Hmm.

08:55:17.733 --> 08:55:20.173
DM: And there's this screech,

08:55:22.273 --> 08:55:24.553
DM: and the waters splash up and

08:55:25.713 --> 08:55:26.313
DM: like

08:55:27.453 --> 08:55:37.653
DM: wipe away this kind of t- tattered remains of a demonic soul, and there's a boom, and this black energy radiates out from where the waters

08:55:37.653 --> 08:55:39.353
DM: crash and hits the magic circle,

08:55:40.593 --> 08:55:43.673
DM: and shanks and doesn't pass the barrier,

08:55:44.933 --> 08:55:46.433
DM: and collapses into the water.

08:55:50.413 --> 08:55:54.393
DM: The scepter gone.

08:55:54.393 --> 08:55:56.173
DM: The entire soul.

08:55:56.173 --> 08:55:57.833
DM: There was no demonic soul.

08:55:57.833 --> 08:56:00.653
DM: It was ripped to shreds by Apollyon.

08:56:00.653 --> 08:56:03.053
DM: It was just a big explosion.

08:56:03.053 --> 08:56:06.533
DM: So all you did with the magic circle was keep you off from taking like

08:56:07.713 --> 08:56:09.613
DM: 15d6 necrotic damage.

08:56:11.313 --> 08:56:11.473
Wellby: Hmm.

08:56:13.393 --> 08:56:15.013
Kenzo: Is the, the being inside is-

08:56:16.033 --> 08:56:17.433
Wellby: Was killed by Apollyon.

08:56:17.433 --> 08:56:17.853
Kenzo: There's nothing left.

08:56:17.853 --> 08:56:18.953
DM: Killed long ago.

08:56:19.813 --> 08:56:20.573
Wellby: Huh.

08:56:20.573 --> 08:56:21.533
DM: In the binding.

08:56:22.893 --> 08:56:28.393
Seeker: And so its soul was powering the scepter, and its soul was destroyed by the holy water

08:56:29.853 --> 08:56:30.273
Seeker: or something?

08:56:30.913 --> 08:56:38.493
DM: What was left of its soul was powering the scepter, but it was long ago shredded and remade by Apollyon into-

08:56:38.513 --> 08:56:38.553
Unknown: Mm

08:56:39.613 --> 08:56:41.433
DM: ... the scepter itself.

08:56:41.433 --> 08:56:48.473
DM: There was nothing of the devilish essence left behind, other than a burst of evil energy as it was destroyed.

08:56:49.113 --> 08:56:56.833
Kenzo: Kenzo, um, as he kind of fled from the circle, is still, like, gripping his staff like super, super tight, like super, super tight.

08:56:56.833 --> 08:57:05.353
Kenzo: Like, processing this, like, intense feeling of having, like, never before having this much power surge through his staff.

08:57:05.733 --> 08:57:06.213
Wellby: Mm.

08:57:06.213 --> 08:57:07.513
Kenzo: Crashing through this thing.

08:57:07.633 --> 08:57:07.813
Wellby: Mm.

08:57:08.093 --> 08:57:11.853
Kenzo: Gripping his staff, gripping it, gripping it, looking at the staff.

08:57:12.653 --> 08:57:13.033
Kenzo: And, um-

08:57:13.033 --> 08:57:14.093
DM: It's like a little

08:57:15.153 --> 08:57:19.173
DM: wave, a curling wave that appears on the top of the staff.

08:57:19.253 --> 08:57:19.913
Kenzo: That's so cool.

08:57:20.253 --> 08:57:21.213
Wellby: Ocean ki.

08:57:22.553 --> 08:57:24.313
Unknown: Holding it, holding it.

08:57:24.313 --> 08:57:24.333
Unknown: Nice.

08:57:24.693 --> 08:57:25.933
Kenzo: Holding it.

08:57:25.933 --> 08:57:31.493
Kenzo: Just feeling the wave, like, kind of pass through him, still passing through him, still passing through him.

08:57:31.493 --> 08:57:33.373
Kenzo: And he's just stunned. He's just kind of

08:57:34.753 --> 08:57:36.633
Kenzo: gripping, barely standing.

08:57:36.633 --> 08:57:46.733
Kenzo: [sighs] Pauses

08:57:46.733 --> 08:57:50.013
Kenzo: for a second and kind of still hasn't, still hasn't opened his eyes.

08:57:50.193 --> 08:57:51.233
Kenzo: He's like, "Is it over?"

08:57:53.153 --> 08:57:54.373
Seeker: I think so.

08:57:54.373 --> 08:57:55.433
Wellby: This part, at least.

08:57:58.353 --> 08:58:01.373
Delwath: Delwath will sort of walk forward and pick his sword up again.

08:58:03.933 --> 08:58:06.613
DM: There's nothing left, no sign of the scepter.

08:58:10.313 --> 08:58:13.613
DM: No sign of any evil here at all.

08:58:19.993 --> 08:58:21.733
Unknown: [sighs] Kenzo gets down on his knees.

08:58:25.913 --> 08:58:29.953
Unknown: Yeah, he's, he's very, very moved by everything that's happened.

08:58:31.213 --> 08:58:32.433
Kenzo: Starts to cry a little bit.

08:58:38.733 --> 08:58:41.373
Kenzo: Was not expecting this past 24 hours to be so intense.

08:58:41.373 --> 08:59:02.033
Kenzo: [sighs]

08:59:02.073 --> 08:59:03.853
Wellby: I think Wellby sighs deep and

08:59:04.993 --> 08:59:09.073
Wellby: shakes something off, and then steps out into the sunlight.

08:59:11.733 --> 08:59:12.553
Kenzo: Were you thinking about it?

08:59:15.173 --> 08:59:17.093
Wellby: No. It's nice not to.

08:59:17.873 --> 08:59:18.113
Kenzo: Yeah.

08:59:18.113 --> 08:59:19.153
Wellby: It's nice not to carry it.

08:59:20.213 --> 08:59:21.113
Seeker: I'm thinking about it.

08:59:22.553 --> 08:59:23.053
Kenzo: Hmm.

08:59:23.053 --> 08:59:27.213
Seeker: I feel a weight lifted to me, from me that I didn't know was on me.

08:59:29.933 --> 08:59:30.073
Kenzo: Hmm.

08:59:31.193 --> 08:59:37.433
Seeker: I'll have to f- find that power that was always just beyond my fingertips in some other way, I suppose.

08:59:38.893 --> 08:59:41.233
Wellby: Not sure that's the lesson to take from this experience.

08:59:41.513 --> 08:59:42.513
Seeker: Sure it is. Sure it is.

08:59:42.513 --> 08:59:45.113
Wellby: [laughs]

08:59:45.293 --> 08:59:47.253
Seeker: Maybe I still have some thinking to do on this.

08:59:50.413 --> 08:59:51.693
Wellby: But Wellby says it with a smile.

08:59:53.513 --> 08:59:57.553
Seeker: It was right there that whole time, and it, it took a toll on me.

08:59:58.093 --> 08:59:58.273
Wellby: Mm.

09:00:01.333 --> 09:00:03.193
Kenzo: Whoa.

09:00:03.193 --> 09:00:04.073
Seeker: What could have been?

09:00:06.573 --> 09:00:15.253
Kenzo: I'm not sure I was ever tempted to use it, but [sighs] I'm very, very, very happy that period,

09:00:16.393 --> 09:00:17.313
Kenzo: that one's gone.

09:00:18.293 --> 09:00:20.053
Seeker: We're free now in a, in another way.

09:00:20.353 --> 09:00:20.513
Wellby: Mm.

09:00:23.773 --> 09:00:25.413
Seeker: This has been our quest for so long.

09:00:26.453 --> 09:00:27.273
Wellby: Better part of a year,

09:00:28.673 --> 09:00:30.313
Wellby: before we even knew this is what it was.

09:00:36.673 --> 09:00:37.253
Kenzo: That being,

09:00:38.793 --> 09:00:39.713
Kenzo: what did it look like again?

09:00:41.553 --> 09:00:42.413
Kenzo: Re, the fiend?

09:00:43.693 --> 09:00:45.053
DM: Uh, it didn't really look like...

09:00:45.053 --> 09:00:47.253
DM: I mean, it didn't really look like much.

09:00:47.253 --> 09:00:50.653
DM: It was, it was tattered and shredded beyond recognition.

09:00:50.673 --> 09:00:50.813
Kenzo: Yeah.

09:00:50.813 --> 09:00:52.873
DM: It was just fragments of a soul that

09:00:53.773 --> 09:00:58.013
DM: shattered outward and hit the magic circle and not you.

09:00:59.433 --> 09:01:01.533
Kenzo: I wonder, I do wonder a little bit about its story,

09:01:02.913 --> 09:01:03.873
Kenzo: whatever that was.

09:01:08.453 --> 09:01:12.693
Delwath: I think its story is lost now, unless we get it from Apollyon.

09:01:16.253 --> 09:01:17.433
Wellby: Where is Apollyon?

09:01:19.733 --> 09:01:20.673
Kenzo: That circular island.

09:01:21.573 --> 09:01:23.013
DM: Near Dranqur, I assume.

09:01:23.693 --> 09:01:24.473
Wellby: On this plane?

09:01:28.233 --> 09:01:29.053
DM: Perhaps not.

09:01:30.973 --> 09:01:32.293
Kenzo: Well, I can take us to the dream world.

09:01:33.413 --> 09:01:33.553
Wellby: Hmm.

09:01:36.153 --> 09:01:37.313
DM: Yeah.

09:01:37.313 --> 09:01:40.973
Kenzo: Tim, uh, Kenzo interacted with Apollyon on the plane of consciousness, right?

09:01:40.973 --> 09:01:41.193
DM: Yep.

09:01:41.593 --> 09:01:41.713
Unknown: Okay.

09:01:46.853 --> 09:01:48.713
Kenzo: He has a presence on multiple planes.

09:01:49.733 --> 09:01:50.913
Kenzo: There's a material presence

09:01:52.033 --> 09:01:52.693
Kenzo: of some kind.

09:02:03.457 --> 09:02:08.237
Seeker: If he could make one scepter, surely he could make another, so this won't stop him for too long.

09:02:10.077 --> 09:02:11.097
DM: Perhaps not.

09:02:12.777 --> 09:02:13.057
DM: He,

09:02:14.077 --> 09:02:17.297
Delwath: he must be substantially weaker now than he was.

09:02:18.137 --> 09:02:18.657
Seeker: Hmm.

09:02:20.577 --> 09:02:23.337
Wellby: Still, Fausta has a scroll to bring planes together.

09:02:25.717 --> 09:02:26.677
Seeker: Oh, that's nothing to worry about.

09:02:26.737 --> 09:02:28.817
Unknown: Yeah, I don't know who would have given him that.

09:02:28.817 --> 09:02:29.837
Kenzo: [laughs]

09:02:29.837 --> 09:02:33.917
Delwath: Seems such a dangerous thing to let into his hand.

09:02:38.637 --> 09:02:40.357
Kenzo: I do recall trying to warn

09:02:43.117 --> 09:02:44.137
Kenzo: at least a few of you,

09:02:45.877 --> 09:02:49.537
Kenzo: but caution isn't necessarily our, uh, forte.

09:02:57.177 --> 09:02:58.957
DM: [laughs] It's true, Kenzo.

09:02:58.977 --> 09:03:00.977
DM: We should have perhaps listened to you.

09:03:00.977 --> 09:03:04.797
Kenzo: [laughs]

09:03:04.797 --> 09:03:06.497
Delwath: But we will not remember next time.

09:03:06.497 --> 09:03:18.457
Kenzo: [laughs]

09:03:18.457 --> 09:03:18.577
Wellby: [laughs]

09:03:18.577 --> 09:03:18.657
Unknown: Oh.

09:03:18.677 --> 09:03:20.117
DM: So as the sun rises

09:03:21.977 --> 09:03:23.277
DM: on the quiet island,

09:03:26.297 --> 09:03:26.497
DM: you,

09:03:27.997 --> 09:03:29.077
DM: you see now the,

09:03:30.297 --> 09:03:33.237
DM: um, in the distance, like sailing to the island,

09:03:34.517 --> 09:03:36.117
DM: a ship, a Skaer ship.

